{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T09:56:19.176Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"897c90c1b80c3e3bf21a36a6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ado-sdk-scalar-normalization"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Expose SDK assignment mutation normalization"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"SDK 2026.10.23 has no public pure assignment-mutation normalizer. sdk/lifecycle/legacy-none-tokens.d.ts:65 declares isLegacyNoneToken(value: string | undefined), but that internal module is absent from package exports; root and sdk/runtime namespaces expose neither isLegacyNoneToken nor normalizeAssigneeMutationInput. Public toNonEmptyImportString handles trimming; normalizeItemMetadata preserves literal assignee strings, whereas native commitItemMutations interprets assignment none/null as clear. previewItemMutations returns ItemMutationPreviewValidation only, without canonical field results; transaction/settings/events/history APIs do not provide a pure equivalent. Open upstream searches normalize assignee and isLegacyNoneToken SDK found no matching issue. Adapter uses the SDK trim primitive plus one centralized clear-token predicate, verified against actual native writes. Title/description none/null remain literal. Missing public export: isLegacyNoneToken or an SDK normalizeAssigneeMutationInput with explicit scalar clear semantics. Orchestrator verifies and files upstream."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["sdk-gap"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created